    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe logic itself is in the right unit \u2014 `formatLocality` sits naturally alongside the existing `format*` default methods, follows their exact null-guard shape, and a derived DTO field belongs in the mapper. The one structural inconsistency is the import convention:\n\n- `OwnerMapper.java:35-36` references `java.util.Map` with fully-qualified names inline (`java.util.Map<String, String> CITY_REGIONS = java.util.Map.of(...)`), but this file already imports every other `java.util` type it uses (`java.util.Collection`, `java.util.List` at lines 15-16). To match the file's established convention, add `import java.util.Map;` and write `Map<String, String> CITY_REGIONS = Map.of(...)`. As written, it reads as foreign against the surrounding declarations and is the kind of thing a maintainer here would normalize on sight.\n\nEverything else (the constant placement next to its sole consumer, the Javadoc depth matching the neighbors, the `@Mapping` wiring, and the OpenAPI schema addition) is coherent and additive.",
